// HUNT D2 - Azure Application Gateway (WAF) logs: multipart / request-body anomalies and 5xx bursts
//
// PREREQUISITE (Azure portal):
//   portal.azure.com > Application gateways > <gateway> > Monitoring > Diagnostic settings > Add diagnostic setting
//   Tick: "Application Gateway Access Log" and "Application Gateway Firewall Log"
//   Destination: Log Analytics workspace, and choose "Resource specific" (so the tables below are AGWAccessLogs / AGWFirewallLogs).
//   If you instead used the legacy "Azure diagnostics" destination, the data is in AzureDiagnostics with *_s/*_d suffixed
//   columns and these queries will not run as written.
//
// WHERE TO RUN: security.microsoft.com > Investigation & response > Hunting > Advanced hunting (or workspace > Logs).
//
// LIMIT: I found no evidence (unverified) of a dedicated Azure WAF managed rule for CVE-2026-109618/109619. The signals below
//   are generic. Cloudflare DOES have named rules (see docs/mitigations.md). Request body content is not logged by Azure WAF.

// ---- Query 1: POST bursts that cause backend 5xx (large bodies + failures) per client ----
AGWAccessLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(14d)
| where HttpMethod == "POST"
| summarize
    Posts = count(),
    Backend5xx = countif(ServerStatus >= 500),
    MaxReceivedBytes = max(ReceivedBytes),
    Uris = make_set(RequestUri, 5),
    Hosts = make_set(Host, 3),
    WafModes = make_set(WafMode)
  by ClientIp, bin(TimeGenerated, 5m)
| where Backend5xx >= 5 and MaxReceivedBytes > 100000
| order by Backend5xx desc

// ---- Query 2: WAF events that mention multipart / body-parsing problems (OWASP CRS 200002 = body parse failure,
//               200003 = multipart strict validation - confirm the IDs in your ruleset version) ----
// AGWFirewallLogs
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(14d)
// | where RuleId in ("200002", "200003") or Message has "ultipart" or DetailedMessage has "ultipart"
// | summarize Hits = count(), Actions = make_set(Action), Rules = make_set(RuleId), Uris = make_set(RequestUri, 5) by ClientIp, bin(TimeGenerated, 10m)
// | order by Hits desc

// ---- Query 3: join the two on TransactionId to see which flagged requests also hurt the backend ----
// AGWFirewallLogs
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(14d)
// | where RuleId in ("200002", "200003") or Message has "ultipart"
// | project TransactionId, RuleId, Message, WafAction = Action
// | join kind=inner (AGWAccessLogs | where TimeGenerated > ago(14d) | project TransactionId, ClientIp, Host, RequestUri, HttpMethod, HttpStatus, ServerStatus, ReceivedBytes) on TransactionId
// | order by ServerStatus desc
